{
  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that pca_n2000 as RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (~0.64 vs ~0.51-0.54 accuracy). However, with scgpt, rna_only multiprofile avgpool (config_008: 0.530) actually outperformed the corresponding multimodal setup (config_002: 0.512), suggesting the image modality may not be adding value with that encoder. The critical open question is whether this pattern holds for pca_n2000: does the image encoder contribute meaningfully on top of an already strong RNA representation? config_022 (rna_only, pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-factor comparison against config_006 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted: 0.639), isolating the effect of the image modality. If rna_only pca_n2000 approaches or exceeds 0.639, it reveals the image is redundant and redirects the search toward simpler RNA-only pipelines; if it falls well below, it confirms the multimodal benefit and justifies further multimodal exploration. Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental design question is more informative than fine-tuning aggregation or fusion within the already-promising multimodal pca_n2000 space."
}

